      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "30a0d072-7837-449e-9db2-228afed80595",
      "key": "270dd11a-0001-4a01-9c01-000000000001",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "preheading",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Academics"
        },
        {
          "alias": "heading",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "JROTC Curriculum Overview"
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "<p>The JROTC curriculum addresses national academic standards, including the Common Core State Standards. It covers leadership, civics, geography and global awareness, health and wellness, language arts, life skills, and U.S. history.</p><p>The curriculum follows performance-based, learner-centred education. Every classroom uses technology to teach, assess, and report progress. Every learning experience addresses core abilities, program outcomes, and course competencies.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
